# Mission 2: Research Interface (WebOps)

## Goal
Enable users to trigger "Deep Research" missions directly from the HUD.
The user enters a topic (e.g., "Mcp servers"), and the **Researcher** agent performs a web search and saving the results.

## User Review Required
None. Internal Mission.

## Proposed Changes

### Backend
#### [MODIFY] [server.py](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/tools/marketing-dashboard/server.py)
- Add `/api/research` endpoint (POST).
- Input: `{"topic": "..."}`.
- Logic: triggers [brain_spawn_agent(intent="Research {topic}", persona="researcher")](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/mcp-server-nucleus/src/mcp_server_nucleus/__init__.py#3661-3716).

### Frontend
#### [NEW] [ResearchWidget.tsx](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/tools/nucleus-hud/app/components/ResearchWidget.tsx)
- Input field ("Enter research topic...").
- "Ignite" button.
- Displays status ("Dispatching Researcher...").

#### [MODIFY] [page.tsx](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/tools/nucleus-hud/app/page.tsx)
- Import `ResearchWidget`.
- Add to the Grid layout (Column 3, below SwarmMonitor).

## Verification Plan
### Automated Tests
- `curl -X POST -d '{"topic": "test"}' http://localhost:9999/api/research` -> 200 OK.
### Manual Verification
- Open HUD.
- Type "Latest AI Trends".
- Click Ignite.
- See "Researcher" spawn in [SwarmMonitor](file:///Users/lokeshgarg/ai-mvp-backend/tools/nucleus-hud/app/components/SwarmMonitor.tsx#14-81).
